<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44171" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sĭdērītis</span></b> ,
		is, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σιδηρῖτις</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Ironwort</i>, <i>vervain</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 25, 5,
				19, § 42</span></i>; <i><span class="en">26, 14, 88, §
			148</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A precious stone</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 37,
				10, 67, § 182</span></i>. A variety of it, found in
			Æthiopia, is called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sĭdērŏpoecĭlos</span></b> ,
			= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σιδηροποίκιλος</span>, <i><span class="en">id. 37, 10,
				67, § 182</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>The loadstone</i>, <i>magnet</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				36, 16, 25, § 127</span></i> Jan.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
